            <article class="policy-card">

                <div class="notice">
                    Please provide the exact URL of the content and a clear explanation of the problem.
                    You do not need to prove your entire legal case before submitting a good-faith report.
                </div>

                <section id="privacy">
                    <h2>1. Privacy / Non-Consensual Intimate Imagery</h2>

                    <p>
                        If content depicts you or contains your private, intimate, sexual, or sensitive
                        information without appropriate consent or authorization, contact:
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        <a href="mailto:support@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org">
                            <strong>support@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org</strong>
                        </a>
                    </p>

                    <p>Reports may include:</p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>non-consensual intimate imagery;</li>
                        <li>private or sensitive material published without authorization;</li>
                        <li>sexual material involving you that should not be publicly available;</li>
                        <li>impersonation or manipulated material depicting you;</li>
                        <li>unauthorized use of your image or likeness; or</li>
                        <li>other serious privacy violations.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        For urgent privacy, NCII, or minor-safety complaints, clearly mark the subject:
                        <strong>URGENT — CONTENT REMOVAL REQUEST</strong>
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="copyright">
                    <h2>2. Copyright Complaint</h2>

                    <p>
                        Copyright owners or authorized representatives should send copyright complaints to:
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        <a href="mailto:dmca@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org">
                            <strong>dmca@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org</strong>
                        </a>
                    </p>

                    <p>A useful copyright report should identify:</p>

                    <ol>
                        <li>the copyrighted work;</li>
                        <li>the URL of the allegedly infringing material;</li>
                        <li>contact information for the reporting party;</li>
                        <li>why the use is believed to be unauthorized;</li>
                        <li>confirmation that the information is accurate and that the reporter is authorized to act,
                            where applicable; and</li>
                        <li>an electronic or physical signature.</li>
                    </ol>

                    <p>
                        Additional information may be requested when reasonably necessary to evaluate the complaint.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="illegal">
                    <h2>3. Illegal or Prohibited Content</h2>

                    <p>
                        Report content that you believe is unlawful or prohibited, including:
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>child sexual abuse material (CSAM) or sexual content involving minors;</li>
                        <li>sexual exploitation or trafficking;</li>
                        <li>non-consensual intimate imagery;</li>
                        <li>unlawful sexual deepfakes or synthetic intimate material;</li>
                        <li>unlawful privacy violations;</li>
                        <li>malware, phishing, fraud, or malicious software;</li>
                        <li>unlawfully obtained personal information; or</li>
                        <li>other material prohibited by applicable law.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Send these reports to
                        <a href="mailto:support@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org">
                            <strong>support@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org</strong>
                        </a>
                        with the relevant URL and enough information to identify the material.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="general">
                    <h2>4. General Abuse / Content Complaint</h2>

                    <p>
                        You may report content that is inaccurate, misleading, unauthorized, incorrectly
                        published, or otherwise problematic.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        General reports should be sent to:
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        <a href="mailto:support@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org">
                            <strong>support@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org</strong>
                        </a>
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        We may review credible reports and may correct, restrict, remove, or otherwise
                        modify access to material where appropriate or required by applicable law.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section id="what-to-send">
                    <h2>5. What to Include in Your Report</h2>

                    <p>
                        To help us process your report efficiently, include:
                    </p>

                    <ol>
                        <li><strong>Content URL:</strong> the exact page or media URL.</li>
                        <li><strong>Reason for the report:</strong> clearly explain what is wrong.</li>
                        <li><strong>Your connection to the content:</strong> for example, copyright owner, depicted
                            person, authorized representative, or other affected person.</li>
                        <li><strong>Relevant details:</strong> identify the specific material and explain why it should
                            be removed or restricted.</li>
                        <li><strong>Contact information:</strong> enough information for us to respond if clarification
                            is required.</li>
                    </ol>

                    <div class="notice">
                        Please do not send unnecessary sensitive personal information. Provide only the
                        information reasonably necessary for us to identify and evaluate your complaint.
                    </div>

                    <p>
                        If the material you previously reported appears again, send the new URL or other
                        identifying information so it can be investigated.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>6. Contact</h2>

                    <h3>General / Privacy / Abuse Reports</h3>

                    <p>
                        <a href="mailto:support@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org">
                            <strong>support@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org</strong>
                        </a>
                    </p>

                    <h3>Copyright Reports</h3>

                    <p>
                        <a href="mailto:dmca@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org">
                            <strong>dmca@viralmmsvideo.dpdns.org</strong>
                        </a>
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        When contacting us, include the relevant URL and a clear explanation of the issue.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <h2>7. What Happens After a Report</h2>

                    <p>
                        Reports may be reviewed manually or with the assistance of automated systems.
                        Automated systems can make mistakes, so credible reports may be reviewed and the
                        relevant material may be corrected, restricted, or removed.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        We may request additional information where reasonably necessary to verify a complaint
                        or determine the appropriate action.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Nothing on this page guarantees removal in every circumstance. Decisions are subject
                        to applicable law and the facts of the particular complaint.
                    </p>
                </section>

            </article>
        </div>
    </main>

